# Prior gaps

Things left "Not covered" or deferred by an earlier run, carried forward so they get tested instead
of quietly forgotten. Every PR run checks this file first (`docs/qa/rules/PR-TEST-RULES.md` §1) for
rows on a surface it touches, tests them, and removes the row — or updates the reason if it's still
blocked.

| Added | From run | Case | Surface | Reason it was Not covered | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Empty is the goal. A long-lived row is a sign something needs unblocking on purpose (a missing
fixture state, a missing test environment), not a permanent excuse.
